			<div class="content" id="post-content-3973631">
									

<blockquote>
<p>Since SCP-4080-1's death, episodes of SCP-4080 regarding <strong>their</strong> life have been re-run, starting at the moment they were born.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Who are &quot;they&quot;:</p>
<ul>
<li>David Kincaid?</li>
<li>Achebe Okoro?</li>
</ul>
<p>IMO it would be more interesting if protagonist of SCP-4080 series would switch to Achebe Okoro post David Kincaid's death.<br />
If series instead restarted from the beginning of late SCP-4080-1's life, pattern of releasing new episode each day about previous day's events would be broken after (presumably) 68 years.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Each new episode is recorded the day before it is broadcasted and consists of a heavily-edited sequence of events that happened to SCP-4080-1 that day.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Just restarting the series feels&#8230; anticlimactic.</p>
<p>-1 for now.</p>

